#  NVIDIA CMP 170HX (GA100) UNDERVOLT CONFIGURATION VIA 170tune


═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
## 0. CONTEXT AND WARNINGS (read before starting)
═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

0.1 **This card.** GA100 mining card 0x20C2, VBIOS 92.00.6D.00.0A, driver 610.43.03, unlocked via cmpunlocker (otherwise the VF range is not open). PCIe SLOT — Gen1/2 x4 (link width x4 is normal, does not affect tuning, but verify the VRAM ceiling: if the card shows <40GB VRAM — memory is NOT unlocked, STOP).

0.2 **Undervolt mechanism:** `nvmlDeviceSetGpcClkVfOffset` (NVML) — NVML requires sudo access. Offset "+X" = the entire VF curve is shifted UP in frequency at the same voltage → same frequency at lower voltage → fewer watts. Second lever — frequency ceiling `nvidia-smi -lgc "210,<max>"`. Both MUST be set.

0.3 **GOLDEN RULE:** "it didn't crash" ≠ stable. Silent compute/memory errors occur without crashes. ANY point MUST be run through the full gate (see Phase 5). No gate = no ship.

0.4 If the card is the only one (GPU 0), all commands without `-i`. On multi-card — specify `-i <idx>`.

0.5 Before starting: backup current state (see Phase 1).

═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
## 1. PRELIMINARY CHECKS
═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

1.1 Check driver, card, VRAM, bank info:
```bash
sudo nvidia-smi
# Expected: Driver 610.43.xx, 1 GPU, >40GB VRAM, P0
```

1.2 Check VF range (CRITICAL):
```bash
sudo /usr/local/bin/nvml_oc   # or nvidia-smi -o VF
```
OUTPUT must show: `GPC allowed range [-1000..+1000] MHz`
If `[0..0]` — card is NOT unlocked. Apply unlock (cmpunlocker driver or hammer), then check again. DO NOT continue with a closed range.

1.3 Check that OTHER PIDs are not holding the GPU:
```bash
sudo nvidia-smi --query-compute-apps=pid,process_name,used_memory --format=csv
```
Must be EMPTY. If something is holding — find the PID, kill it (for testing).

1.4 Check NVML: `sudo ldconfig -p | grep nvml` → must show `libnvidia-ml.so`.
If not — `sudo pip(apt) install nvidia-ml` or move lib to `/lib/os`.

═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
## 2. BACKUP CURRENT STATE (mandatory! recovery in case of trouble)
═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

2.1 `mkdir /root/hwd_backup`

2.2 Save full state:
```bash
sudo nvidia-smi -q > /root/hwd_backup/state_before_$(date +%Y%m%d).txt
```

2.3 Record what is running: service IP, PIDs of external applications (vLLM, etc.), its launch command (`ps aux | grep vllm`) for restarting.

2.4 In `/root/hwd_backup/restore.sh` create a rollback script:
```bash
sudo nvidia-vf-derate --reset 2>/dev/null;   # reset VF
sudo nvidia-smi -lgc 210,1695;               # max ceiling just in case
sudo nvidia-smi -pl 300;                     # open PL
sudo nvidia-smi -rac -rmc -rgc;              # reset locks/clocks
reboot
```

2.5 For full rollback later: `reboot` (the card always boots STOCK — profile is applied AFTER boot, so bricking is impossible).

═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
## 3. INSTALL 170tune (or verify tool compatibility)
═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

3.1 Clone and build the TOOL (using 170tune: a ready-made harness with gitlab safety prompts):
```bash
if [ ! -d /opt/170tune ]; then
    sudo git clone https://github.com/cachenetics/170tune /opt/170tune
    cd /opt/170tune && sudo ./install.sh
else
    echo "170tune already exists, just update" # git pull; ./install.sh
fi
```
EXPECTED: 16 ok (or 16/16), folders `/usr/local/sbin/*`

3.2 Check tuning readiness:
```bash
sudo 170tune preflight
```
Expected: all `[ok]`, except one bottom item (FBPA privilege masks) — it may be closed if unlock is not with the PLM matrix. DO NOT proceed to memory-MCLK if this FAILS — but SM undervolt works without it (NVML path).
Record STOCK_NDIV, STOCK_REFRESH from the output — compare later.

