## 4. STOCK SNAPSHOT (one-time, permanent)
═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

4.1 `sudo 170tune snapshot-stock`
Creates `/var/lib/170tune/stock/<serial>.conf` with the card's true factory values (NDIV/refresh/timings). This is the rollback reference.

4.2 Ensure GPU is free during tuning.

═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
## 5. BASELINE (stock → numbers BEFORE)
═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

5.1 `sudo 170hx-oc stock`   # remove any current offsets, keep stock

5.2 Measure: `sudo oc_eff 10`
→ should print: `offset=0 pl=?W | bf16=<X> TFLOPS P=<Y>W sm=<Z>MHz GFOPS/W Tmax=...`
Record X (TFLOPS), Y (watts), Gz (GFLOPS/W), T (temp).
Typical stock: ~185 TF / 195W / 950 G/W / 55°C.
This is the reference for comparison. If errors appear at baseline CM=0 — unlock is broken.

═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
## 6. CHOOSE TARGET POINT
═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

6.1 Ready-made profiles (from stock): dense +250/1200, eff +300/1350, match +250/1400, balanced +300/1470, perf +350/1590, max +350/1650.

6.2 Reference efficiency values from the docs (DOWNLOAD from https://github.com/cachenetics/170tune/tree/main/docs/measurement-matrix.md):
+250/1350 ~132W / +300/1350 ~131W / +250/1200 ~120W / +300/1200 ~119W

6.3 Selection criteria for WEAK cooling:
- PREFERRED: start with +250/1350 (~34% power savings at ~0% loss)
- If cooling is very weak (temp >80°C when throttled) — +250/1200
- DO NOT START with +300 — first verify at a lower point via gate (see 7)

6.4 REMEMBER: the machine is NOT the same as in the docs. LOCAL silicon may:
- reject the point (silent errors) → back off offset by 50
- accept with MARGIN → can increase by 50-100.

═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
## 7. FULL GATE (CORE OF THE PROCESS — DO NOT SKIP)
═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

7.1 For point (off, clk): e.g. +250/1350:
```bash
sudo 170tune gate 250 1350 4
```
THIS IS: 4 runs of pattern-sweep across ALL VRAM (write→readback bit-exact)
+ 45sec bit-exact GEMM compute-check, each with HBM warmup to 60°C.
Expected success: 4× "sweep N: mem_errors=0 compute_ok=1"
+ "compute: ... 0 comparison rounds bad".

7.2 IF OUTPUT: "mem_errors≠0" or "SILENT COMPUTE CORRUPTION" —
← point is UNACCEPTABLE. STEP DOWN:
- reduce the cell: 250→200/1350 or 250→1200
- REPEAT gate. Never apply "close enough".

7.3 IF all 4 passed: record the win: "GATE PASSED for +X/clk".

7.4 IMPORTANT NOTE: sweep is HOT at 60°C HBM — because silent errors only manifest when heated. If the gate is cold (35-40°) — it lies.

═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
## 8. WORKLOAD RANK (verification with REAL load)
═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

8.1 Ready solution (if vLLM is already running on the same machine as an NLP service):
```bash
sudo 170tune gate 250 1350 2 --workload sudo -u <user> bash \
    /usr/local/bin/vllm_workload_check.sh
```
(script from 170tune, starts/stops vllm.service itself)

8.2 More flexible option (recommended):
- LAUNCH vLLM in the background with the same arguments that worked before
- Wait for /health — OK
- Run your bench: `python benchmark_vllm.py <model>`
- Verify GPU is back: `nvidia-smi --query gpu --stats power/clock/temp`
- Ensure the server REMAINS alive after the load.
Success = all requests passed + server alive + no Xid in dmesg.

8.3 The point: sweep+GEMM may pass, but the real vLLM pattern may crash it. Only the combination (sweep + workload) gives confidence.

