## 9. CONFIRMATION VIA oc_eff (efficiency)
═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

9.1 After profile, confirm savings:
```bash
sudo 170hx-oc custom 250 1350   # or '170hx-oc eff' if +300 passed
```

9.2 `sudo oc_eff 10`
Compare with Phase 5.
EXPECTED for +250/1350: ~180 TF at ~131W → GFLOPS/W ~1376
(35-45% improvement in GFLOPS/W from stock).

9.3 Check power/temp: `nvidia-smi --query-gpu=power.draw,temperature.gpu --format=csv`

═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
## 10. PERSISTENCE (surviving reboots)
═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

10.1 Save profile to persist (requires receipt from gate 7.x):
```bash
sudo 170tune persist save --offset 250 --clk 1350
```
If saved: "saved /var/lib/170tune/persist/<serial>.conf"

10.2 Enable at boot:
```bash
sudo 170tune persist enable
```
Verify: `systemctl is-enabled 170tune-persist` → enabled.
NOTE: this does NOT touch power-limit. Separate power-limit tuner (see 11).

10.3 VERIFY generation:
```bash
sudo 170tune persist status
```

═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
## 11. POWER LIMIT (consciously paired with frequency)
═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

11.1 QUICK TEST: tuning on VF+clock. PL is not primary — acts as a failsafe.
Do not set PL below the consumed power of the undervolt (otherwise frequency oscillates). For +250/1350 → PL 150-200.

11.2 Set: `sudo nvidia-smi -pl <W>`
Verify: `nvidia-smi -q -d POWER | grep "Power Limit"`
For insertion into systemd/kernel: create a oneshot unit 'nvidia-power-limit' (instructions in "Creating a service" section below).

11.3 EDGE: PL at 300 (VBIOS max) is also OK for this profile (frequency ceiling). If you want to minimize risk with weak cooling — set PL slightly above the profile's consumed power (at 150-200W).

═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
## 12. POST-REBOOT VALIDATION (mandatory)
═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

12.1 `reboot`

12.2 After boot: `sudo 170tune persist status` → EXPECTED: profile active
And mandatorily:
```bash
sudo /usr/local/bin/nvml_oc | grep "current offset" → +250
nvidia-smi --query-gpu=clocks.max.graphics,power.limit,memory.total --format=csv
```
(limit should be what you set in the unit, speed and VRAM intact)

12.3 REPEAT real workload run easily for 3-5 min (see 8) — because after reboot GSP switches → something may become unstable.

12.4 Check for errors: `dmesg | grep -i 'NVRM: Xid'` must remain EMPTY

═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
## 13. ROLLBACK (if something broke)
═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

- Stock in 7 hits: `sudo 170hx-oc stock` + `sudo nvidia-smi -pl <your stock>`
- If GPU responds/video-crash: `sudo reboot` (will boot stock — profile may not apply)
- If service broke: `sudo systemctl mask 170tune-persist.service; reboot`
- If loading/unloading: full rollback: `reboot` → step 2 (restore.sh)

═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
## 14. WHAT NOT TO DO (warnings in advance)
═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

- DO NOT push OPENED NVIDIA VF past +450 without checking (hard GPU crash, requires power cycle).
- DO NOT raise memory NDIV (HBM) on this card with weak cooling, and DO NOT even try `-lmc 1000` (doesn't work — NVML path is closed, and the real ndiv lever heats terribly (crash at >76 NDIV)).
- DO NOT accept results without FULL gate.
- After undervolt DO NOT run bitfix only on IG.
- DO NOT return to closed APIs from abdolj — unauthorized access is NOT supported, and memory DAMAGE is entirely at our own risk, and only after gate.
- DO NOT execute this protocol on an unverified machine (not preflighted).

